    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the PR!\r\n\r\nI don't think this is a good fit for 'mini.extra' at least for the following reasons:\r\n- There is already very similar functionality in ['mini.basics'](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/44a3ab2bc6b40edeb7a76359826c9779d5c70cb5/doc/mini-basics.txt#L239) under `gV` mapping. Yes, it is only for Visual mode, but it feels usually enough for this particular case. Maybe, should have it in Operator-pending mode there also :thinking: \r\n- It is fairly compact and straightforward to have in one's config verbatim.\r\n\r\nClosing as \"not the best fit for 'mini.extra'\".",
            "created_at": "2025-01-18T13:37:01Z",
