        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "@echasnovski No problem! Do you think it would be worth including a `fold` text object on `mini.extra`? Here’s what I currently have in my configuration:\r\n```lua\r\nz = function(ai_type)\r\n  local foldlevel = vim.fn.foldlevel(vim.fn.line \".\")\r\n  if foldlevel <= 0 then\r\n    return\r\n  end\r\n  vim.cmd.normal { \"zxzc\", bang = true }\r\n  local start_line = vim.fn.foldclosed(vim.fn.line \".\")\r\n  local end_line = vim.fn.foldclosedend(vim.fn.line \".\")\r\n  vim.cmd.normal { \"zo\", bang = true }\r\n  if ai_type == \"i\" then\r\n    start_line = start_line + 1\r\n    end_line = end_line - 1\r\n  end\r\n  return {\r\n    from = { line = start_line, col = 1 },\r\n    to = { line = end_line, col = 1 },\r\n    vis_mode = \"V\",\r\n  }\r\nend,\r\n```",
            "created_at": "2025-01-18T13:41:57Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/pull/1492#issuecomment-2599722463",
            "id": 2599722463,
