        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Do you think it would be worth including a `fold` text object on `mini.extra`? Here’s what I currently have in my configuration:\r\n\r\nIn theory - maybe, but there is no good/\"proper\" way of dealing with folds in Neovim (yet). Having to close and open fold is not something I'd be comfortable having in 'mini.extra'. Maybe custom line traversing up and down while inspecting their `vim.fn.foldlevel()` would be good, but... Having to have *extensive* testing for many fold methods for this textobject doesn't bring me joy.\r\n\r\nI feel bad for denying second time in less than 30 minutes, but let's not have it in 'mini.extra'. Maybe in the future when there is a 'mini.folds' or similar. Huge thanks for the enthusiasm, though!",
            "created_at": "2025-01-18T13:56:48Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/pull/1492#issuecomment-2599726900",
